<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices on Thursday remained steady in central Indian markets and plant delivery condition in limited trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 2,000 tonnes on low business volumes, they said. Soyoil prices was also steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady but there was litte trade. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $284 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction $112 per tonne in export and was 3,850-3,900 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>&quot;More than 60 percent processing plants have been closed down as availability of soybean was very poor. Remaining plants were running on 20-25 percent capacity at present. Capacity utilisation was around 80-100 rupees per tonne at the same time last year,&quot; said a leading soybean trader.</p>
